{"module":"housing-today","voice":"female","duration":162.4,"segments":[{"el":"title","text":"Housing today: evictions, screening and keeping homes","start":0.0,"end":3.95,"words":[[0.05,0.51],[0.51,0.98],[1.25,1.94],[2.21,2.76],[2.76,2.99],[2.99,3.37],[3.37,3.76]]},{"el":"intro","text":"Redlining and urban renewal are history (see “Place” and “Burned, flooded and taken”).","start":4.75,"end":10.48,"words":[[4.8,5.51],[5.51,5.74],[5.74,6.06],[6.06,6.61],[6.61,6.69],[6.69,7.24],[7.24,7.4],[7.4,7.79],[7.79,8.03],[8.03,8.42],[8.7,9.17],[9.17,9.41],[9.41,9.96]]},{"el":"intro","text":"This lesson is about what keeps families from stable homes now.","start":10.83,"end":14.54,"words":[[10.88,11.08],[11.08,11.4],[11.4,11.53],[11.53,11.86],[11.86,12.06],[12.06,12.32],[12.32,12.77],[12.77,13.03],[13.03,13.49],[13.49,13.82],[13.82,14.08]]},{"el":"h0","text":"Evictions","start":14.89,"end":16.0,"words":[[14.93,15.79]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Princeton's Eviction Lab has found that Black renters, especially Black women, face eviction filings far out of proportion to their share of renters.","start":16.7,"end":26.2,"words":[[16.75,17.44],[17.44,17.98],[17.98,18.21],[18.21,18.44],[18.44,18.82],[18.82,19.05],[19.05,19.36],[19.36,19.89],[20.16,20.77],[20.77,21.08],[21.08,21.54],[21.81,22.11],[22.11,22.65],[22.65,23.19],[23.19,23.34],[23.34,23.57],[23.57,23.72],[23.72,24.33],[24.33,24.49],[24.49,24.72],[24.72,24.95],[24.95,25.1],[25.1,25.64]]},{"el":"s0","text":"An eviction record makes it harder to rent again.","start":26.55,"end":29.52,"words":[[26.6,26.73],[26.73,27.22],[27.22,27.56],[27.56,27.9],[27.9,28.04],[28.04,28.31],[28.31,28.45],[28.45,28.73],[28.73,29.07]]},{"el":"s0","text":"In 2017 New York City became the first city to guarantee tenants facing eviction a lawyer; several cities and states, including San Francisco, Washington, Maryland and Connecticut, have followed.","start":29.87,"end":43.45,"words":[[29.93,30.08],[30.08,31.09],[31.09,31.31],[31.31,31.53],[31.53,31.82],[31.82,32.25],[32.25,32.4],[32.4,32.69],[32.69,32.98],[32.98,33.13],[33.13,33.63],[33.63,34.14],[34.14,34.58],[34.58,35.09],[35.09,35.23],[35.23,35.59],[35.85,36.28],[36.28,36.65],[36.65,36.87],[36.87,37.37],[37.63,38.21],[38.21,38.43],[38.43,39.23],[39.48,40.13],[40.39,41.04],[41.04,41.26],[41.26,41.99],[42.24,42.46],[42.46,42.97]]},{"el":"h1","text":"Laws that punish calling 911","start":44.35,"end":47.49,"words":[[44.4,44.66],[44.66,44.91],[44.91,45.33],[45.33,45.75],[45.75,47.35]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Many cities adopted “nuisance” or “crime-free housing” ordinances that penalize landlords, and push them to evict tenants, after a certain number of police calls to a property.","start":48.19,"end":59.22,"words":[[48.24,48.54],[48.54,48.93],[48.93,49.46],[49.46,50.0],[50.0,50.08],[50.08,50.69],[50.69,51.15],[51.15,51.84],[51.84,52.07],[52.07,52.68],[52.68,53.37],[53.64,53.87],[53.87,54.1],[54.1,54.33],[54.33,54.49],[54.49,54.87],[54.87,55.48],[55.75,56.06],[56.06,56.21],[56.21,56.59],[56.59,56.98],[56.98,57.13],[57.13,57.51],[57.51,57.82],[57.82,57.97],[57.97,58.13],[58.13,58.74]]},{"el":"s1","text":"In Norristown, Pennsylvania, Lakisha Briggs was threatened with eviction after police were called during domestic violence attacks against her; she sued, the city repealed its ordinance and settled in 2014.","start":59.57,"end":73.56,"words":[[59.62,59.77],[59.77,60.55],[60.82,61.83],[62.1,62.57],[62.57,62.95],[62.95,63.19],[63.19,63.73],[63.73,63.96],[63.96,64.51],[64.51,64.82],[64.82,65.2],[65.2,65.36],[65.36,65.67],[65.67,66.21],[66.21,66.83],[66.83,67.45],[67.45,67.84],[67.84,68.31],[68.31,68.54],[68.81,68.97],[68.97,69.28],[69.55,69.7],[69.7,70.01],[70.01,70.48],[70.48,70.71],[70.71,71.25],[71.25,71.49],[71.49,71.95],[71.95,72.11],[72.11,73.04]]},{"el":"s1","text":"HUD warned in 2016 that such ordinances can violate fair housing law.","start":73.91,"end":79.46,"words":[[73.96,74.2],[74.2,74.53],[74.53,74.7],[74.7,75.76],[75.76,76.01],[76.01,76.33],[76.33,77.07],[77.07,77.32],[77.32,77.97],[77.97,78.22],[78.22,78.71],[78.71,78.96]]},{"el":"s1","text":"They are the mirror image of the CAREN problem: some people are punished for calling police, while others call police as a weapon.","start":79.81,"end":86.68,"words":[[79.87,80.07],[80.07,80.14],[80.14,80.28],[80.28,80.55],[80.55,80.89],[80.89,81.03],[81.03,81.16],[81.16,81.5],[81.5,82.05],[82.29,82.49],[82.49,82.83],[82.83,82.9],[82.9,83.31],[83.31,83.44],[83.44,83.78],[83.78,84.19],[84.43,84.7],[84.7,84.98],[84.98,85.18],[85.18,85.52],[85.52,85.66],[85.66,85.79],[85.79,86.2]]},{"el":"h2","text":"Screening by algorithm","start":87.58,"end":89.64,"words":[[87.63,88.33],[88.33,88.63],[88.63,89.54]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Landlords increasingly rely on tenant-screening scores.","start":90.34,"end":94.29,"words":[[90.38,91.01],[91.01,91.8],[91.8,92.19],[92.19,92.35],[92.35,93.38],[93.38,93.77]]},{"el":"s2","text":"In 2024 SafeRent Solutions agreed to pay about $2.3 million to settle a Massachusetts lawsuit alleging its scores unfairly rejected Black and Hispanic applicants who used housing vouchers.","start":94.64,"end":107.71,"words":[[94.69,94.84],[94.84,95.89],[95.89,96.49],[96.49,97.09],[97.09,97.46],[97.46,97.61],[97.61,97.84],[97.84,98.21],[98.21,99.26],[99.26,99.71],[99.71,99.86],[99.86,100.23],[100.23,100.38],[100.38,101.21],[101.21,101.58],[101.58,102.11],[102.11,102.33],[102.33,102.63],[102.63,103.15],[103.15,103.83],[103.83,104.13],[104.13,104.35],[104.35,104.95],[104.95,105.62],[105.62,105.77],[105.77,106.07],[106.07,106.52],[106.52,107.12]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Many states and cities now ban rejecting applicants just because they use a voucher.","start":108.06,"end":113.05,"words":[[108.11,108.37],[108.37,108.77],[108.77,108.97],[108.97,109.31],[109.31,109.51],[109.51,109.71],[109.71,110.31],[110.31,110.91],[110.91,111.24],[111.24,111.57],[111.57,111.77],[111.77,111.97],[111.97,112.1],[112.1,112.57]]},{"el":"h3","text":"The ownership gap","start":113.95,"end":115.33,"words":[[114.0,114.18],[114.18,114.84],[114.84,115.12]]},{"el":"s3","text":"About 45% of Black households own their homes, compared with about 73% of non-Hispanic white households (Census Bureau).","start":116.03,"end":124.92,"words":[[116.08,116.42],[116.42,117.38],[117.38,117.52],[117.52,117.8],[117.8,118.48],[118.48,118.69],[118.69,118.89],[118.89,119.31],[119.55,120.03],[120.03,120.23],[120.23,120.57],[120.57,121.67],[121.67,121.81],[121.81,122.56],[122.56,122.84],[122.84,123.53],[123.53,123.94],[123.94,124.49]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Lower appraisals (see “Banking”), higher mortgage costs and less family wealth for down payments keep the gap wide.","start":125.27,"end":131.55,"words":[[125.32,125.6],[125.6,126.23],[126.23,126.37],[126.37,126.86],[127.1,127.38],[127.38,127.8],[127.8,128.15],[128.15,128.36],[128.36,128.57],[128.57,128.99],[128.99,129.27],[129.27,129.41],[129.41,129.68],[129.68,130.24],[130.24,130.45],[130.45,130.59],[130.59,130.8],[130.8,131.15]]},{"el":"s3","text":"In 2022 a federal task force (PAVE) issued an action plan on appraisal bias.","start":131.9,"end":137.57,"words":[[131.95,132.1],[132.1,133.1],[133.1,133.25],[133.25,133.75],[133.75,134.03],[134.03,134.25],[134.25,134.54],[134.79,135.08],[135.08,135.22],[135.22,135.58],[135.58,135.86],[135.86,136.01],[136.01,136.58],[136.58,137.01]]},{"el":"h4","text":"Keeping families housed","start":138.47,"end":140.2,"words":[[138.48,138.93],[138.93,139.56],[139.56,140.02]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Right to counsel in eviction court.","start":140.9,"end":142.95,"words":[[140.95,141.19],[141.19,141.32],[141.32,141.74],[141.74,141.87],[141.87,142.29],[142.29,142.54]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Repeal crime-free and nuisance ordinances that punish calls for help.","start":143.3,"end":147.59,"words":[[143.35,143.73],[143.73,144.33],[144.33,144.55],[144.55,145.08],[145.08,145.75],[145.75,145.97],[145.97,146.35],[146.35,146.65],[146.65,146.8],[146.8,147.17]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Source-of-income protections for voucher holders.","start":147.94,"end":150.84,"words":[[147.97,148.63],[148.63,149.29],[149.29,149.42],[149.42,149.81],[149.81,150.34]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Down-payment help and community land trusts that keep homes affordable for good.","start":151.19,"end":155.77,"words":[[151.23,151.96],[151.96,152.22],[152.22,152.42],[152.42,153.02],[153.02,153.28],[153.28,153.68],[153.68,153.88],[153.88,154.07],[154.07,154.4],[154.4,154.93],[154.93,155.07],[155.07,155.33]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Heirs' property help so families keep inherited homes and land (a pro bono quest).","start":156.12,"end":161.46,"words":[[156.17,156.38],[156.38,156.89],[156.89,157.18],[157.18,157.39],[157.39,157.9],[157.9,158.12],[158.12,158.77],[158.77,159.13],[159.13,159.34],[159.34,159.63],[159.63,159.78],[159.78,160.07],[160.07,160.5],[160.5,160.93]]}]}